10
00:00:25.830 --> 00:00:29.300
And I wanted to do that just because, I mean,

11
00:00:29.300 --> 00:00:30.530
they have over 50 million viewers.

12
00:00:30.530 --> 00:00:33.000
It goes worldwide and the military can get it as well.

13
00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:33.833
It did.

14
00:00:33.833 --> 00:00:35.300
I've always done a lot of things for USO

15
00:00:35.300 --> 00:00:36.472
and people like that, but...

16
00:00:36.472 --> 00:00:38.722
(applause)

17
00:00:41.280 --> 00:00:43.630
But, it's fun, it's an evening with,

18
00:00:43.630 --> 00:00:45.330
and one of the things that I wanted to do,

19
00:00:45.330 --> 00:00:47.630
especially coming out of this pandemic

20
00:00:47.630 --> 00:00:50.800
and people starting to perform again, Drew, is

21
00:00:50.800 --> 00:00:54.320
to me, you know how you play different characters?

22
00:00:54.320 --> 00:00:56.710
I play different vocal styles

23
00:00:56.710 --> 00:00:59.440
and it's been a lifetime of learning how to do it,

24
00:00:59.440 --> 00:01:01.090
from, you know, country to jazz,

25
00:01:01.090 --> 00:01:04.940
to pop to legit soprano, to belt, to operatic.

26
00:01:04.940 --> 00:01:07.150
It's really, really challenging,

27
00:01:07.150 --> 00:01:08.870
and it's been my goal to do that.

28
00:01:08.870 --> 00:01:11.190
So in this show, you're just gonna get a little sampling.

29
00:01:11.190 --> 00:01:13.060
It's not my full symphonic show,

30
00:01:13.060 --> 00:01:17.763
but we have a full symphonic orchestra and music.

31
00:01:18.840 --> 00:01:22.140 line:15%
When you hear it in that context where everything is live,

32
00:01:22.140 --> 00:01:24.750 line:15%
it hits everything from your chakras to the tones,

33
00:01:24.750 --> 00:01:27.690
