34
00:01:27.690 --> 00:01:32.350
And it is so fun. I have video from six decades.

35
00:01:32.350 --> 00:01:34.970
It's just, you'll hear everything that...

36
00:01:34.970 --> 00:01:37.120
I mean, it's a super fun show.

37
00:01:37.120 --> 00:01:40.360
Download it, it's free, and you'll get a little taste

38
00:01:40.360 --> 00:01:42.420
of some of the songs from the album too.

39
00:01:42.420 --> 00:01:46.980
Now, your latest album is "Unexpected".

40
00:01:46.980 --> 00:01:50.440
That is the title. That is beautiful, by the way.

41
00:01:50.440 --> 00:01:51.487
That's, that I...

42
00:01:51.487 --> 00:01:54.526
I have a child calling me on my phone? Hold on.

43
00:01:54.526 --> 00:01:55.480
(Marie laughs)

44
00:01:55.480 --> 00:01:56.880
Okay. There, I've turned it off.

45
00:01:56.880 --> 00:01:57.811
There we go.

46
00:01:57.811 --> 00:02:00.970
I so feel you right now.

47
00:02:00.970 --> 00:02:02.487
I always keep it there in case they need me

48
00:02:02.487 --> 00:02:03.500
and I'll go, are you okay?

49
00:02:03.500 --> 00:02:05.310
Yes. Okay, I'll call you back.

50
00:02:05.310 --> 00:02:06.450
Well, that's depressed...

51
00:02:06.450 --> 00:02:09.480
But anyway, I was in Vegas and my son called me

52
00:02:10.350 --> 00:02:13.740
and I hit, I'll talk to you later.

53
00:02:13.740 --> 00:02:15.705
And then I never did.

54
00:02:15.705 --> 00:02:16.538
(audience sighs)

55
00:02:16.538 --> 00:02:18.690
So, sorry.

56
00:02:18.690 --> 00:02:20.970
No. I, I...

57
00:02:20.970 --> 00:02:24.010
So it's something that is very important to me

58
00:02:24.010 --> 00:02:26.453
to always have my phone on for my children.

59
00:02:27.550 --> 00:02:29.360
I'm so sorry that that happened.

60
00:02:29.360 --> 00:02:30.897
No, you know what?

61
00:02:30.897 --> 00:02:34.150
It's one of those things that you go through.

62
00:02:34.150 --> 00:02:38.530
I lost my son. He was 18.

63
00:02:38.530 --> 00:02:41.110
And I'm really good. I'm okay.

64
00:02:41.110 --> 00:02:43.380
It's just every now and then, you know, people say,

65
00:02:43.380 --> 00:02:44.220
do you ever get over it?

66
00:02:44.220 --> 00:02:45.423
No, you never do.

67
00:02:46.400 --> 00:02:49.140
But God gives you respites and that's...

68
00:02:49.140 --> 00:02:50.400
you hit triggers.

69
00:02:50.400 --> 00:02:52.680
That just happened to be a trigger. Sorry about that.

70
00:02:52.680 --> 00:02:55.800
No, I totally understand.
Yeah.

71
00:02:55.800 --> 00:02:56.670
I really do.

72
00:02:56.670 --> 00:02:59.530
Our lives are full of triggers

73
00:02:59.530 --> 00:03:04.170
and they come up at the most unexpected times,

74
00:03:04.170 --> 00:03:05.630
speaking of the title.
Exactly.

75
00:03:05.630 --> 00:03:08.520
Can I ask if it's possible

76
00:03:08.520 --> 00:03:11.300
to ask you a piece of life advice

77
00:03:11.300 --> 00:03:14.780
that when something does throw you

78
00:03:14.780 --> 00:03:15.950
I know what you're gonna say.

79
00:03:15.950 --> 00:03:19.230
and rock your world, like it just did,

80
00:03:19.230 --> 00:03:22.000
how beautifully you just handled it

81
00:03:22.000 --> 00:03:24.693
and there's people out there,

82
00:03:26.272 --> 00:03:31.272
I'm just wondering if you have any life advice

83
00:03:31.670 --> 00:03:36.340
for how one might be able to handle a trigger.

84
00:03:36.340 --> 00:03:41.260
Ooh, well, I think that God never gives you

85
00:03:41.260 --> 00:03:42.970 line:15%
anything that you can't handle.

86
00:03:42.970 --> 00:03:44.590 line:15%
I don't know that God gives them to you,

87
00:03:44.590 --> 00:03:46.750 line:15%
but I know that people have agency

88
00:03:46.750 --> 00:03:49.160 line:15%
to make choices that affect you.

89
00:03:49.160 --> 00:03:54.160
And I believe that when life is too much to stand,

90
00:03:54.710 --> 00:03:58.840
I get on my knees and I beg, and I just know,

91
00:03:58.840 --> 00:04:02.160
somehow He gives you that comfort with my son.

92
00:04:02.160 --> 00:04:04.100
You know, a lot of people judged me very harshly

93
00:04:04.100 --> 00:04:05.890
that I went back to work.

94
00:04:05.890 --> 00:04:09.480
You understand that, Drew, you know, you're kind of...

95
00:04:09.480 --> 00:04:11.350
You do everything on a national level

96
00:04:11.350 --> 00:04:13.070
instead of a private level

97
00:04:13.070 --> 00:04:16.010
within your community or whatever.

98
00:04:16.010 --> 00:04:19.380
But I had to choose to go back to work

99
00:04:19.380 --> 00:04:23.540
because I had seven more children that were hurting

100
00:04:23.540 --> 00:04:27.430
and they needed to know that you had to keep living life.

101
00:04:27.430 --> 00:04:31.410
And so, and I felt that was something

102
00:04:31.410 --> 00:04:32.920
that I wanted to do for them,

103
00:04:32.920 --> 00:04:34.550
despite what people were saying.

104
00:04:34.550 --> 00:04:35.383
Thank you.

105
00:04:35.383 --> 00:04:38.920
I'm very, very grateful for your answer and your candor.

106
00:04:38.920 --> 00:04:41.999
And I agree with the fight and I thank you.

107
00:04:41.999 --> 00:04:44.582
(upbeat music)

